# Paths Semgrep skips. Replaces Semgrep's built-in default list, which would
# otherwise skip `src/test/java`.
#
# That replacement only happens when this file sits at the project root Semgrep
# resolved, and Semgrep resolves that root from git — which is the monorepo
# root, not `backend/`. So `scripts/semgrep.sh` passes `--project-root .` to
# pin the root to this directory. Without that flag this file is read but the
# built-in defaults stay in force and every test source is silently skipped.
#
# Two consequences of pinning the root here:
#   - patterns resolve against `backend/`, so a path outside it cannot be named;
#   - the monorepo's root `.gitignore` is no longer consulted, so anything
#     generated must be listed below rather than relied on being git-ignored.

# Generated and vendored output
graphify-out/
node_modules/
target/

# Local secrets — real credentials, and not ours to print in a finding
.env

# Rule-test fixtures: every `ruleid:` line in them is a finding by design. scripts/semgrep.sh
# runs them through `semgrep --test` instead, which names its targets explicitly.
semgrep/tests/
